      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like the [reference manual has an equation for how quickly the TRNG produces random numbers](https://www.st.com/resource/en/reference_manual/dm00314099-stm32h742-stm32h743-753-and-stm32h750-value-line-advanced-arm-based-32-bit-mcus-stmicroelectronics.pdf#page\u003d1264).\n\n[`Section 34.5 RNG Processing Time`](https://www.st.com/resource/en/reference_manual/dm00314099-stm32h742-stm32h743-753-and-stm32h750-value-line-advanced-arm-based-32-bit-mcus-stmicroelectronics.pdf#page\u003d1272).\n\nI\u0027m not sure offhand what we\u0027re setting as the frequency for the two clocks it lists; you\u0027ll have to check the EC source code.\n\nFor bloonchipper, it\u0027s a bit simpler:\n\n[`15.5 RNG Processing Time`](https://www.st.com/resource/en/reference_manual/dm00180369-stm32f412-advanced-arm-based-32-bit-mcus-stmicroelectronics.pdf#page\u003d407)\n\nbut you\u0027ll still need to check to see what we\u0027re setting the RNG clock to.",
